# The JAXA 30P30N three-element section, meshed the way its own reference mesh is:
# a structured near-wall ribbon on every surface, unstructured triangles outside.
#
# WHAT THIS IS MATCHED AGAINST, and the numbers it is held to, are in
# docs/research/jaxa-30p30n-reference-mesh.md -- which measured the reference
# project file itself (20 structured ribbons of ~1.5% chord, 206,370 quads;
# 1,011,462 triangles outside them; 1.22 M cells over x in [-5,4], y in [-5,3]).
#
# THE RIBBON DEPTH, and what used to cap it. 0.0038 chord here is a quarter of
# the reference's 0.015. It used to be forced: two fronts growing into each
# other aborted the whole run, and this file recorded it as "builds at 0.0038,
# fails at 0.0042 with Critical proximity detected after retreat".
#
# THAT CAP IS GONE. Two geometries' fronts that meet now FREEZE the nodes
# involved and the layer tapers to zero there, which is what the published
# practice does when a front cannot advance -- it stops that node, not the run
# (docs/research/meshing-the-cove-and-the-trailing-edges.md; gated by
# tools/PreProcessor/tests/test_bl_front_meeting.py). Re-measured 2026-11-02:
# this section builds at BL_LAYERS 120, i.e. 0.0089 chord, 1,214,780 cells,
# exit 0, with one warning naming the slot at (0.8767, 0.0249) where the taper
# starts -- at layer 9 of 123, so that stretch was always going to be thin.
# 160 layers still fails, on a DIFFERENT condition: one geometry's own front
# self-intersecting, which is the convex-cusp rule and not this one.
#
# BL_LAYERS stays at 60 so this shipped case keeps its size and its cost. The
# depth is now a choice rather than a cap; raise it if you want the ribbon.
LENGTH_UNIT custom
LENGTH_UNIT_METRES 0.4572          # the stowed chord, so lengths here are chords
MESH_MODE 0

DOMAIN_X_MIN -5.0
DOMAIN_X_MAX  4.0
DOMAIN_Y_MIN -5.0
DOMAIN_Y_MAX  3.0

SURFACE_MESH_SIZE 0.004
AUTO_SURFACE_SIZE 1
FARFIELD_MESH_SIZE 1.0
# 0.014 is derived, not tuned by eye: the size field is LINEAR in the distance
# from the boundary-layer front, so this rate is what puts ~0.0034 chord at the
# distance where the reference's near field reads ~0.0039.
FARFIELD_GROWTH_RATE 0.014

# 60 layers, first cell 5.4e-5 chord, growth 1.005 -> 0.0038 total. The near
# uniform normal spacing is the reference's own: its ribbons run 0.2 to 2.2 in
# last-over-first interval, not the 50-100x of a stretched layer.
BL_INITIAL_THICKNESS 0.00005446
BL_GROWTH_RATE 1.005
BL_LAYERS 60

BL_CONVEX_METHOD 0
BL_FAN_NODES 5
BL_AUTO_FAN_NODES 1
BL_FAN_ANGLE_THRESHOLD 60.0
BL_CONCAVE_METHOD 5
BL_CONCAVE_ANGLE_THRESHOLD 120.0
BL_TRANSITION_LAYERS 3
BL_TRANSITION_GROWTH_RATE 1.15
BL_TRANSITION_BUFFER 2.0
GMSH_ALGORITHM 6
GMSH_OPTIMIZE 1
ENABLE_COLLISION_DETECTION 1

EXPORT_VTK 1
EXPORT_STARCD 1
BC_GEOM wall
BC_XMIN inlet
BC_XMAX outlet
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/30p30n_jaxa_slat.dat
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/30p30n_jaxa_main.dat
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/30p30n_jaxa_flap.dat
OUTPUT_FILENAME results/meshes/hybrid_30p30n/mesh_hybrid_30p30n.vtk
